          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What GST applies to transport services in Mumbai?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "GTA road freight: 5% under RCM (paid by recipient) or 5%/12% under FCM (chosen by GTA). Courier: 18% with ITC. Freight forwarding: 18%. Warehousing: 18% (agri exempt). Air cargo: 18%. Sea freight import: 5% RCM. Classification depends on consignment note issuance (GTA vs non-GTA)."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does RCM work for GTA freight in Mumbai?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "When GTA provides freight to registered factory, company, or GST-registered person, recipient pays 5% GST. GTA doesn't collect or remit. Recipient self-invoices via GSTR-3B. No ITC at 5%. Alternatively, GTA opts FCM by March 15 declaration: 5% (no ITC) or 12% (with ITC). Patron evaluates RCM vs FCM."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does logistics accounting cost in Mumbai?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Single-branch operator: Rs 10,000-20,000/month. Multi-branch: Rs 25,000-60,000. JNPT forwarder: Rs 20,000-50,000. 3PL/warehousing: Rs 25,000-75,000. Large enterprises: Rs 75,000-2,50,000."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is e-way bill mandatory for all goods movement?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Mandatory for goods above Rs 50,000 - interstate and intrastate in Maharashtra. Generated before movement. Part A (invoice/consignment) + Part B (vehicle). Valid for specific distances. Violation: Rs 10,000 penalty or tax + penalty, plus goods/vehicle detention under S.129 CGST."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can small fleet owners use presumptive taxation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. S.44AE for up to 10 goods carriages: Rs 1,000/ton gross weight per month per vehicle. No books required. No tax audit. Heavy goods vehicles only. Above 10 vehicles: regular books + S.44AB audit. Patron assesses which is more tax-efficient."
          }
        },
