<!-- SECTION 2: OVERVIEW / INTRO + TL;DR -->
<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Logistics & Transport Accounting in Mumbai - Overview</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Logistics Transport Accounting in Mumbai Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>Logistics accounting covers <strong>GTA GST (RCM 5% / FCM 5% or 12%)</strong> under SAC 9965, <strong>e-way bill</strong> management (&gt; Rs 50,000), <strong>fleet depreciation</strong>, <strong>JNPT customs duty</strong>, <strong>warehousing GST</strong> (18%; agri exempt), multi-modal freight, and transport payroll. Post-Sep 2025: 12% rationalised to 18% (with ITC); 5% (no ITC) remains for concessional.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper" style="margin-top:16px;"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Governing Acts</td><td>GST (SAC 9965, Notif 13/2017 RCM); Customs Act 1962; Motor Vehicles Act; Maharashtra MVT Act</td></tr><tr><td>Applicable To</td><td>GTAs, freight forwarders, 3PL, fleet owners, warehousing, customs brokers, couriers</td></tr><tr><td>Timeline</td><td>GST monthly; e-way bill per consignment; TDS quarterly; PTRC by 15th</td></tr><tr><td>Cost From</td><td>Rs 10,000/month (single-branch operator)</td></tr><tr><td>Penalty</td><td>GST: Rs 50/day; e-way bill: Rs 10,000 or tax + penalty; vehicle detention</td></tr><tr><td>Authority</td><td>GST Commissionerate Mumbai; JNPT Customs; Income Tax; RTO Maharashtra</td></tr></tbody></table></div></p>
                </div>
                <p>Mumbai is India's logistics nerve centre. <strong>JNPT</strong> handles 50%+ of containerised cargo. <strong>Bhiwandi</strong> = Asia's largest warehousing hub. <strong>Mumbai Port Trust</strong> for bulk cargo. <strong>Andheri Air Cargo Complex</strong>. <strong>Mumbai-Pune Expressway</strong> = busiest freight route. GTA GST at 5% (RCM) or 12% (FCM with ITC). E-way bill for &gt; Rs 50,000. Learn more about <a href="#">Logistics Accounting across India</a>.</p>
                <p>Patron's Marine Lines office handles GST Commissionerate, JNPT Customs, and IT Department filings. Also see <a href="/accounting-services/mumbai">Accounting Services in Mumbai</a> and <a href="/gst-registration/mumbai">GST Registration in Mumbai</a>.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Logistics & Transport Accounting</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Specialised financial management of freight operators, fleet owners, warehousing companies, and supply chain businesses - covering <strong>GTA GST (RCM/FCM, SAC 9965)</strong>, <strong>e-way bill</strong> documentation, <strong>fleet depreciation</strong>, <strong>customs duty</strong>, and multi-modal revenue tracking. For Mumbai logistics: consignment-note-based revenue, <strong>RCM liability tracking</strong>, and JNPT customs reconciliation.</p><p>A Bhiwandi GTA: RCM 5% (recipient pays) or FCM 12% (with ITC, declaration by March 15). A JNPT forwarder: customs duty (BCD + IGST + SWS), shipping bills, CFS charges. A Bhiwandi 3PL: warehouse GST 18% (agri exempt), e-way bill per dispatch &gt; Rs 50,000. A fleet owner with 50 trucks: vehicle-wise depreciation S.32, Maharashtra MVT, fuel/tyre allocation per trip. <strong>Each model = distinct accounting.</strong></p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Logistics Transport Accounting in Mumbai:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>GTA RCM:</strong> Recipient pays 5% GST. GTA doesn't collect. For factories, companies, registered persons. No ITC at 5%.</p><p><strong>GTA FCM:</strong> GTA collects GST. 5% (no ITC) or 12% (with ITC). Declaration by March 15. Valid entire FY.</p><p><strong>E-Way Bill:</strong> Mandatory &gt; Rs 50,000. Part A (invoice) + Part B (vehicle). Violation: Rs 10,000 or tax + penalty. Detention S.129 CGST.</p><p><strong>S.44AE:</strong> Presumptive for ≤ 10 goods carriages. Rs 1,000/ton/month. No books. No audit.</p><p><strong>SAC 9965:</strong> GTA 5%/12%. Courier 18%. Freight forwarding 18%. Warehousing 18% (agri exempt).</p>

                </div>
            </div>
