                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What GST applies to transport services in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>GTA road freight: 5% under RCM (paid by recipient) or 5%/12% under FCM (chosen by GTA). Courier: 18% with ITC. Freight forwarding: 18%. Warehousing: 18% (agri exempt). Air cargo: 18%. Sea freight import: 5% RCM. Classification depends on consignment note issuance (GTA vs non-GTA).</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How does RCM work for GTA freight in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>When GTA provides freight to registered factory, company, or GST-registered person, recipient pays 5% GST. GTA doesn't collect or remit. Recipient self-invoices via GSTR-3B. No ITC at 5%. Alternatively, GTA opts FCM by March 15 declaration: 5% (no ITC) or 12% (with ITC). Patron evaluates RCM vs FCM.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does logistics accounting cost in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Single-branch operator: Rs 10,000-20,000/month. Multi-branch: Rs 25,000-60,000. JNPT forwarder: Rs 20,000-50,000. 3PL/warehousing: Rs 25,000-75,000. Large enterprises: Rs 75,000-2,50,000.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is e-way bill mandatory for all goods movement?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Mandatory for goods above Rs 50,000 - interstate and intrastate in Maharashtra. Generated before movement. Part A (invoice/consignment) + Part B (vehicle). Valid for specific distances. Violation: Rs 10,000 penalty or tax + penalty, plus goods/vehicle detention under S.129 CGST.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can small fleet owners use presumptive taxation?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. S.44AE for up to 10 goods carriages: Rs 1,000/ton gross weight per month per vehicle. No books required. No tax audit. Heavy goods vehicles only. Above 10 vehicles: regular books + S.44AB audit. Patron assesses which is more tax-efficient.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can logistics companies get accounting done online?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. GTA GST, e-way bill monitoring, fleet depreciation, JNPT customs, trip-wise MIS all handled digitally. Walk-in at Marine Lines for operators from Bhiwandi, Navi Mumbai, Andheri Cargo Complex.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Transport pe GST kitna?</strong> GTA freight: 5% (RCM) ya 12% (FCM with ITC). Courier: 18%. Warehousing: 18%. Air freight: 18%.</p><p><strong>E-way bill kab banana padta hai?</strong> Rs 50,000 se upar ke goods pe mandatory - interstate aur intrastate dono.</p><p><strong>Chhote fleet owner ko books rakhne padte hain?</strong> Nahi - 10 gaadi tak S.44AE pe presumptive. Usse zyada pe regular books + audit.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
